'From Pharo13.1.0SNAPSHOT of 29 August 2025 [Build information: Pharo-13.1.0+SNAPSHOT.build.697.sha.af10a2ce70915e5076b7c9664f7851b9f7d95376 (64 Bit)] on 7 July 2026 at 10:49:40.213461 pm'!CMCell subclass: #ECECVegetationUnit	uses: TCMMath	instanceVariableNames: 'biomass'	classVariableNames: ''	package: 'ECEC-Model'!!ECECVegetationUnit commentStamp: '2026-07-07T17:17:04.433861+02:00' prior: 0!VegetationUnit is the Cell class of ECEC. The model consists of a two-dimensional grid, wrapped in both axes to avoid edge effects. The Plants are created only once and have a fixed location. They do not move, die, or reproduce. A plant’s only “behaviors” is to grow (and be eaten by foragers). The plants vary only in their biomass, which represents the amount of food energy available to foragers. At each time unit, this biomass level increases according to a discrete logistic growth:Biomass(t+1) = Biomass(t) + r.Biomass(t) . [1 - Biomass(t) / K]If biomass is the main attribute of VegetationUnit, r and K and class variables (their values are the same for all the plants a given simulation)!!ECECVegetationUnit methodsFor: 'converting' stamp: '2025-09-15T15:30:06.154356+02:00'!asString	" Private - See superimplementor's comment " 	^ String streamContents: [ : stream |  		  stream 			  << super asString; 				crtab; tab; 			 	<< 'biomass: '; 				<< (biomass truncateTo: 0.005) asString ]! !!ECECVegetationUnit methodsFor: 'accessing' stamp: '2025-09-15T15:30:06.155324+02:00'!biomass	^ biomass! !!ECECVegetationUnit methodsFor: 'accessing' stamp: '2025-09-15T15:30:06.155636+02:00'!biomass: anObject	biomass := anObject! !!ECECVegetationUnit methodsFor: 'growth' stamp: '2025-09-15T15:30:06.155936+02:00'!growBiomass	<action>	self biomass: (self logisticGrowth: self biomass r: self class r k: self class k)! !!ECECVegetationUnit methodsFor: 'initialization'!initialize 	super initialize.	biomass := 0! !!ECECVegetationUnit methodsFor: 'initialization' stamp: '2025-09-15T15:30:06.15783+02:00'!initializeWithRandomBiomass	self biomass: self random! !!ECECVegetationUnit methodsFor: 'pov'!povBiomass	<pov>	^ CMPointOfView color: (CMColor		colorValue: biomass		min: 0		max: self class k		color: Color green)! !!ECECVegetationUnit methodsFor: 'pov' stamp: '2025-09-15T15:30:06.158813+02:00'!povBiomassForager		<pov>	^ self biomass < ECECForager catabolicRate		ifTrue: [ CMPointOfView color: Color white ]		ifFalse: [ self povBiomass ]! !!ECECVegetationUnit methodsFor: 'pov' stamp: '2025-09-15T15:30:06.159341+02:00'!povForagersVision	<pov>	(self hasOccupantsOfClass: ECECForager)		ifTrue: [ ^ self povBiomassForager ].		(self neighbourhood anySatisfy: [ :each | each hasOccupantsOfClass: ECECForager ])		ifTrue: [ ^ self povBiomassForager ].		^ CMPointOfView color: Color black! !!ECECVegetationUnit methodsFor: 'stepping'!step		self growBiomass! !"-- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- "!ECECVegetationUnit class	uses: TCMMath classTrait	instanceVariableNames: 'k r'!!ECECVegetationUnit class commentStamp: '2026-07-07T17:17:04.433861+02:00' prior: 0!VegetationUnit is the Cell class of ECEC. The model consists of a two-dimensional grid, wrapped in both axes to avoid edge effects. The Plants are created only once and have a fixed location. They do not move, die, or reproduce. A plant’s only “behaviors” is to grow (and be eaten by foragers). The plants vary only in their biomass, which represents the amount of food energy available to foragers. At each time unit, this biomass level increases according to a discrete logistic growth:Biomass(t+1) = Biomass(t) + r.Biomass(t) . [1 - Biomass(t) / K]If biomass is the main attribute of VegetationUnit, r and K and class variables (their values are the same for all the plants a given simulation)!!ECECVegetationUnit class methodsFor: 'parameters'!k	<parameterIntegerDefault: 10>	^ k! !!ECECVegetationUnit class methodsFor: 'parameters' stamp: '2025-09-15T15:30:06.151857+02:00'!k: aNumber	<parameterSetter>	k := aNumber! !!ECECVegetationUnit class methodsFor: 'parameters'!r	<parameterFloatDefault: 0.2>	^ r! !!ECECVegetationUnit class methodsFor: 'parameters' stamp: '2025-09-15T15:30:06.152136+02:00'!r: aNumber	<parameterSetter>	r := aNumber! !